 1. @@count set in Base, read through Sub                      0
 2. Sub.bump does @@count += 1 -- Base.count / Sub.count       1 / 1
 3. Sub assigns @@count = 100 -- Base.count / Sub's own?       100 / false (class_variables(false))
 4. an instance method reads @@count                           100
 5. an instance method assigns @@count = 7 -- Base.count       7
 6. class-level @count_ivar -- Base's / Sub's                  0 / nil
 7. @@items = []; Sub.push(1) -- Base.items                    [1]
 8. class_variable_get / class_variables / defined?(:@@nope)   7 / [:@@count, :@@items] / false
 9. Base.class_variable_get(:@@nope)                           NameError: uninitialized class variable @@nope in Base
10. @@fresh set in Early, then in Base -- Early.fresh          RuntimeError: class variable @@fresh of Early is overtaken by Base
11. @@count read at the top level, outside any class           RuntimeError: class variable access from toplevel
